<title>USA: Florida $10 mln Housing Finance Agency priced.</title>
<headline>Florida $10 mln Housing Finance Agency priced.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merrill Lynch &amp; Co said it priced a $10 million Florida Housing Finance Agency multi-family housing revenue bond issue with a top yield of 6.30 percent in 2036.</p>
<p>The bonds are AMBAC insured and rated Aaa by Moody's Investors Service and AAA by Standard &amp; Poor's Corp.</p>
<p>The bonds are dated 9/1/1996 and the first coupon is 3/1/1997. The bonds are due 9/1.</p>
<p>The firm said it had received the verbal award and the account is closed.</p>
<p>The bonds are callable 9/1/2006 at 102.00, declining to par on 9/1/2008.</p>
<p>The bonds are priced at par.</p>
<p>PRICING SCALE</p>
<p>	9/1	   Amount	  Coupon	Price</p>
<p>    Maturity	(mln)	   (pct)	 (% of par)</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    2010	    $1.225	  5.85	  100.00</p>
<p>    2016	    $1.010	  6.10	  100.00</p>
<p>    2026	    $2.800	  6.20	  100.00</p>
<p>    2036	    $5.655	  5.30	  100.00</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
